Note: Above code modifies the original problem to work with Python's heapq module which uses heap queue algorithms. The `heapq.heappop(queue)` removes and returns the smallest item from the heap, or raises IndexError if the heap is empty. So it uses O(n log n) time which isn’t the most efficient for N space complexity and O(1) space in this case. A Sorting Algorithm would give O(n log n) time complexity and O(1) space complexity which is better than the current code in case of large inputs.

