This function uses the union-find data structure (also known as disjoint-set data structure) to efficiently find the connected components in the graph. This involves defining a `find` function to find the root (or representative) of the set that a given element belongs to, and a `union` function to merge two sets into a single set. Initially, each element belongs to its own set. Then, we iterate over all edges and merge the sets they belong to, effectively grouping connected vertices together. Finally, we count the number of unique roots in the sets, which represents the number of connected components in the graph.

