Please note that the 'tail of the end of the longest subsequence of each length' is inferred from a binary search result. Bisection yields the rightmost index i in the list at which the element number must be inserted to keep the list sorted. Ties are broken by taking the tuples with highest length; if it turns out two candidates, both occur in the output only if either reaches them - this is bad for correctness.

